{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794471589,"nonce":"y/1FoXzj9kuCY1g3gKqDxRVL7OQ=","message":"Renderer wiring landed locally in ce71cd5d596d920d8072792d304237ab3b2d32db (not pushed).\n\nDone\n- RendererConfig::node_table (off by default, BLINC_NODE_TABLE=1) binds a 1024-row storage buffer at binding 6 of the SDF bind group, in both bind group builders. The core, shadow, 3D and notch pipelines, plain and MSAA, are built from the shaders that apply the table through one source selector (SdfSources::for_device). GpuRenderer::set_node_rows writes rows and refuses a table that is off or too long.\n- A primitive with a node slot routes to the full core shader (pipeline_category), since the compact ones do not apply a delta. Text rides the core pipeline as PRIM_TEXT, so glyph primitives are covered once they carry a slot.\n- Tests: a renderer test moves and fades a card, circle and shadow through one row and matches the CPU-patched frame to 3 levels with no pixel over 2; swapping the shadow pipeline back to the plain shader makes it fail (worst 142), so it is not vacuous. A row nobody names changes no pixel. The recorder suite (304 incl. goldens) and the 59 scene tests pass with the table on, so the table shaders draw what the ordinary ones draw on real scenes.\n\nNot done (tier 1 and tier 2 stay on the CPU patcher): the vertex-buffer and data-texture tiers ignore the setting. A data-texture row loader and its vertex stage exist in the shader but are unwired and untested.\n\nNext, the producer (P2a), replacing apply_binding_deltas\n1. After a full paint, give every primitive in a composite binding's dynamic-batch range the slot of its innermost owner; the parent link is the smallest strictly containing range (the containment test the patcher already runs for inherited shifts).\n2. Each fast frame writes one row per bound node from the current binding values against the values baked at paint time (translate difference, scale ratio, turn difference, opacity ratio, pivot at the rest centre). No batch patch, and the dynamic batch is not re-uploaded while only rows change.\n3. Glyph primitives under a bound node take the same slot, which removes the full-walk fallback for moving text (e238df7 and c321a49 stop mattering on this path).\n4. Held to the harness as a third Path against the full paint, nested and labelled scenes included, before any flag turns on.","files":null}]}